    "description": "•\tContractor at Elizabeth City, NC Coast Guard Base. \n•\tCreate SAS programs to run reports from ALMIS to Oracle.\n•\tDesign, analyze, develop, and implement database objects in Oracle.\n•\tCreating database tables, views, indexes, procedures, sequences, and triggers for PHP and Oracle Forms and Reports.\n•\tCreating and execute Oracle procedures to populate tables with data, such as pdf files and Access data through directories created in Oracle for PHP and Oracle Forms and reports.\n•\tAll the views and procedures I create I must make sure they run under a minute and if they don’t I have to tune them so they will by troubleshooting the code. \n•\tMonitor my errors using all_errors plus monitor tablespace use through Enterprise Manager to ensure I don’t run out of room.\n•\tLoad Oracle tables, indexes, sequences, triggers, and procedures using a Unix shell script.\n•\tWrite test plans for QA and Stage to follow.\n•\tCreate product insert and implementation instructions for all projects \n•\tCommunicate with fellow developers and the customer to ensure the reports are correct. \n•\tCreate data maps in Erwin and pdf files.\n•\tNormalize Ingres and Oracle tables.\n•\tConverting the Ingres database to an Oracle 10g database. \n•\tCreate temporary tables in the database to pull data from the DWS database to update the Ingres employee and Coast Guard base tables.\n•\tCreating database procedures for Ingres.\n•\tCreating database tables, views, indexes, procedures and packages with temporary tables and cursors for Oracle so Cognos/Business Intelligence can create reports from the procedures.\n•\tCreating Oracle tables, views, indexes, procedures and tables to convert Application Forms (.rw and .osq) so the Cognos/ Business Intelligence can create reports from the procedures.\n•\tWorking with DBA’s to create a new development Oracle database to make sure tablespace size is correct and users have correct privileges.\n•\tUse SAS to import data to Oracle tables.",
